[how to uncancel a lich]
> The most straightforward way is to kill a creature and resurrect it.
> This will get rid of cancellation.
> Of course it's rather unreliable for monsters that only have a
> _chance_ to leave a corpse, and it's completely impractical for
> liches, who are guaranteed _not_ to leave one

A quick wizmode test (well, a somewhat fiddly wizmode test) reveals
that stoning a creature and then stone-to-fleshing it is equally
effective at uncancelling. Any stoneable monster will reliably leave
a statue, and that includes liches; so provided you can cast stone
to flesh, this seems to me to be a reliable way to uncancel a lich.

Whether it'll still be tame once you've done it is another question.
